 @KentonBenfield  So for a practical example: my 3080 12G is underclocked and volted and consumes ~250 Watt per hour. I can therefore play 4 hours to get 1kWh or 3.600.000 Joule. But to make use of this example given here, I have to convert Joules into Watt which is a bit stupid, because 1 Joule equals 0,000000278 kWh. Without calculator it's a bit rough and I actually dont want to pull out my smartphone/calculator every time I want to know how much power something draws in a given time.
In a mathematical way it may make sense, in a practical way not so much, because my energy provider doesnt care about joules, they account me for kWh.
That beeing said: I'm out, as this makes no sense to me as a non-mathematics student...

